### Implementation issue

Failed message will be serialized wrapped in `SerializedEnvelopeMessage` by the failure transport, which will make it impossible to handle in the future. Sure the message was not deleted, it is still unusable by the application.

### About the approach

This feels like we are trying to bridge two approaches.
1 - `TransportInterface` serializing
2 - Middleware serialization
Even if we don't implement the full middleware based serialization, being sure we want to go this way would ensure we are not adding more complexity in a component showing design issues.

Lets consider what we now need to add a new transport: a `TransportInterface` implementation which must now use a `SerializerInterface`. Previously, it wasn't required.
Lets consider all the potential states an envelope can now have: full PHP object with non-sendable stamps, serialized, full PHP object with sendable stamps only. These states can all transit through the middleware stack without being properly documented.

I worry we are adding accidental complexity rather than reducing it.

