I still think a clean result type would be cleaner than an exception. Something like `Envelope<object{...}|object{error:Throwable,raw:string}>` would be good enough. No existing transport need to care about that one. Only the middleware throwing the throwable and the serializer need to care about these changes.

So library adding transports don't need to update, library adding serializer only need to update if they care about decoding failure in theory.

Also, I'd argue `PhpSerializer` is already shipping decoding failures on the `Envelope` in some cases: https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/8c1ab342d3ee5dc53a2c33f222a1ea5331e11106/src/Symfony/Component/Messenger/Transport/Serialization/PhpSerializer.php#L110C1-L111C1
